From 5b0d7e20ef441ad4eedb8411d6923ed63c72a485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:10:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dialogue): translate Bedrock NPC conversations into Java
 dialogs

Handle protocol 2193 NPC dialogue with Java built-in dialogs so ordinary
Java clients can use server conversations through ViaProxy. Preserve the
server action indices while hiding opening and closing command entries.
Send indexed NPC requests instead of executing transmitted commands locally.

Bind responses to one active scene and its tracked actor, reject stale or
invalid actions, and clear the dialog when the NPC disappears. Share busy
screen checks with forms and inventory. Link actions use Java URL prompts.

A Bedrock Dedicated Server 1.26.51.1 probe confirms fixed-width actor IDs,
JSON modes and indices, entry requests, branching button requests, and exit
requests with the original scene name. Focused tests cover packet layouts,
scene replacement, request ordering and shared screen state.

Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 (build 51061372, protocol 2193) also sends
ExecuteOpeningCommands for scenes without on-open actions. A branching BDS
conversation records indexed selection, closing the original scene, then
opening the replacement even when its action list contains only a button.
Acknowledge every accepted scene instead of deriving entry requests from
the presence of command entries.

Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 (build 51061372, protocol 2193) sends an
empty scene, name, dialogue and action JSON on ordinary NPC interaction.
Use the tracked actor's NAME_RAW_TEXT (112), NAME (4), INTERACT_TEXT
(100) and ACTIONS (41) when those unnamed packet fields are absent.
The matching BDS reference renders the raw display name over NAME and
literal newlines, selects the original metadata action index, and sends
opening, indexed selection and closing requests with an empty scene.
Keep named scene values authoritative even when empty, and do not merge
an explicit empty action array with stored actions. Read current metadata
on each open and retain stale response rejection across replacements.

Keep no-button conversations valid for clients without the add-on by
using a notice dialog with the same exit response. Java's multi-action
dialog codec rejects an empty action list; the native add-on scene path
remains independent of this compatibility presentation.

Retain a separately authorized editor session and type the NPC request
data field. Pinned native build 51061372/protocol 2193 sends SetName (3),
SetSkin (4), SetInteractText (5), and whole-list SetActions (0) with an
empty scene name, even when a named dialogue opened the editor. Keep
student selections and command execution separate from editing, preserve
LF text, validate action modes and bounds, and reject stale editor IDs.
The native creative operator editor does not execute student exit actions.

Validate command wire text separately from editable text: native action
serialization appends a terminal LF. Permit that terminator after 1,024
editable characters without accepting oversized command or URL content.
